# Desktop UI (macOS, Linux, Windows)

**Folder:** `lib/desktop/` only. One UI codebase, three native runners: `macos/`, `linux/`, `windows/`.

## Structure

```
lib/desktop/
  design/desktop_tokens.dart    # min window size, pane widths, title-bar spacing
  layout/desktop_layout_scope.dart
  screens/*_body.dart
  widgets/
    shell/                      # DesktopShellScaffold, menu bar, side rail / split view
    catalog/
    reader/
    common/
```

## Conventions

- Activated via `useDesktopShell(context)` — native desktop only, **never** `kIsWeb`.
- **Desktop ≠ Web:** no `WebSidebar`, no browser-style layout.
- **Desktop ≠ Mobile:** no bottom tab bar, no phone FAB on large windows.
- Use keyboard shortcuts, resizable panes, context menus, mouse hover.
- Share brand tokens from `lib/design/`; layout numbers live in `DesktopTokens`.

## Shell guard

```dart
bool useDesktopShell(BuildContext context) {
  if (kIsWeb) return false;
  switch (defaultTargetPlatform) {
    case TargetPlatform.macOS:
    case TargetPlatform.linux:
    case TargetPlatform.windows:
      return true;
    default:
      return false;
  }
}
```

Route order in `lib/screens/`: **web → desktop → mobile**.

## Runner config vs UI

- Window icons, entitlements, CMake/msix → `macos/`, `linux/`, `windows/`.
- All widget/layout code → `lib/desktop/`.

Verify: `make reader-run-macos`, `reader-run-linux`, `reader-run-windows`.
